# Sophistication Q1: What single auxiliary motion (before, during, or after the core action) would most strengthen this cue? State where it occurs and why.
# A head turn away from the viewer, which occurs at the very end of the sequence. This gaze aversion acts as a social follow-through, breaking eye contact and reinforcing the finality of the cancellation, making the gesture more socially meaningful and less purely mechanical.
# Sophistication Q2: How should the full `movements` sequence change to incorporate that auxiliary motion while preserving the core cue? If no useful extra motion is needed, write "n/a".
# The original sequence (pose -> head_shake -> arm_retract) will be preserved, and a new `movement` step will be added at the end for the head to pan to the side. A small hold time will be added after the arm retraction to create a distinct beat before this final head turn.

# Q1: How would a human perform this motion? (One sentence)
A human would first shake their head 'no', then pull their extended hand back towards their body, possibly looking away to signal the finality of the decision.
# Q2: Pose Candidates Comparison. Rank at least 2 pose configurations (torso_height, arm_position, gripper_orientation, head, left_arm, x/y/z) and state the winner and why—do NOT pick presets from gesture names alone.
# Candidate 1: `arm_position: "front"`, `gripper_orientation: "vertical"`, `torso_height: "mid"`. This is a clear, neutral "offer" pose, similar to initiating a handshake, which makes its cancellation unambiguous.
# Candidate 2: `arm_position: "front"`, `gripper_orientation: "horizontal"`. This is more specific to offering an object on a palm-up hand.
# Winner: Candidate 1, because its general nature makes the subsequent "cancel" action broadly applicable and easy to understand.
# Q3: Structure Comparison. Compare 2+ full primitive sequences (e.g., M1: pose > movement > pose vs M2: pose > path > path). State the winner and why—**prioritize movement/path beats that express the cue**, not pose-only tweaks.
# Structure 1: `pose` (offer) -> `movement` (head shake) -> `path` (arm retract). This is the original, clear sequence.
# Structure 2: `pose` (offer) -> `movement` (head shake) -> `path` (arm retract) -> `movement` (head pan away). This adds a final beat of social disengagement.
# Winner: Structure 2. The added head turn provides a strong, socially legible follow-through that punctuates the cancellation and makes the entire gesture more expressive and definitive.
# Q4: Context Reinforcement. Compare 2+ micro-timing choices (speed, repetition, hold_time, torso/head expression) that make the gesture read stronger and pick the best one.
# Choice 1: A fast head shake (speed 3.0) followed by a slower arm retraction (speed 1.0) and a moderate head turn away. This contrast highlights the sharp "no" followed by a more deliberate physical and social withdrawal.
# Choice 2: All movements are fast. This would make the gesture read as more abrupt or even angry.
# Winner: Choice 1. The varied timing creates a more nuanced and intentional-feeling gesture, separating the negation signal from the act of retraction and final disengagement.
{
  "cue": "cancel_previous_offer_retract",
  "description": "Cancels an offer by shaking its head 'no', retracting the extended arm, and then turning its head away to finalize the refusal.",
  "movements": [
    {
      "type": "pose",
      "duration": 0.5,
      "parameters": {
        "pose": {
          "torso_height": "mid",
          "arm_position": "front",
          "gripper_orientation": "vertical",
          "head": "center",
          "z": 40
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "movement",
      "duration": 0.8,
      "parameters": {
        "movement": {
          "joints": [
            {
              "joint": "head",
              "axis": "pan",
              "degrees": [
                -15,
                15
              ]
            }
          ],
          "repetition": 2,
          "speed": 3.0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "path",
      "duration": 1.0,
      "parameters": {
        "path": {
          "mode": "ee",
          "shape": "line",
          "axis": "x",
          "distance": -0.25,
          "speed": 1.0,
          "hold_time": 0.2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "movement",
      "duration": 0.5,
      "parameters": {
        "movement": {
          "joints": [
            {
              "joint": "head",
              "axis": "pan",
              "degrees": -30
            }
          ],
          "speed": 1.2
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
